<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T July N+A naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T July N+A naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has tendered to buy 28,000-tonnes of naphthenic and aromatic (N+A) naphtha for delivery July 20-31 to Kaohsiung, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender closes May 28 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>CPC's last tender, for May 11-31 delivery, was awarded at just below $230 per tonne on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
